1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,003
Gold fell 24.6 percent in 60 days.

2
00:00:03,003 --> 00:00:05,577
The worst period since 1982.

3
00:00:05,577 --> 00:00:08,283
But isn't gold supposed to be safe? Silver fell even worse.

4
00:00:08,283 --> 00:00:10,387
More than 15 percent in just one week.

5
00:00:10,387 --> 00:00:13,701
Your jewellery. Your gold loan. Your gold fund.

6
00:00:13,701 --> 00:00:17,844
The value of everything shook. Understand today where the mistake happens.

7
00:00:17,844 --> 00:00:21,164
Why does the safest thing get sold first? The answer is at the end.

8
00:00:21,164 --> 00:00:23,746
And the reason that nobody tells you.

9
00:00:23,746 --> 00:00:27,621
Today, 3 questions. First, how far can gold and silver fall? Second,

10
00:00:27,621 --> 00:00:29,946
why did they fall suddenly? Third, your jewellery,

11
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:33,434
gold loan and gold fund, what will happen to them now?

12
00:00:33,434 --> 00:00:34,636
First, let's talk about the price.

13
00:00:34,636 --> 00:00:37,340
In the world, gold's price is set in dollars,

14
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:38,842
per ounce.

15
00:00:38,842 --> 00:00:41,846
An ounce is the international unit for weighing gold, like our tola.

16
00:00:41,846 --> 00:00:44,958
For months this price stayed above 3,500 dollars.

17
00:00:44,958 --> 00:00:47,136
People thought of it as a strong wall. They thought,

18
00:00:47,136 --> 00:00:48,692
what could go lower than this now.

19
00:00:48,692 --> 00:00:50,870
Then this very November, that wall broke.

20
00:00:50,870 --> 00:00:54,011
Within one day, gold slid sharply. So low,

21
00:00:54,011 --> 00:00:56,839
that it hadn't gone that low in the last 15 months.

22
00:00:56,839 --> 00:00:59,980
The market became restless. But this fall was not sudden.

23
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:01,224
The shock reached India too.

24
00:01:01,224 --> 00:01:04,211
Here, the price of gold is tied to this world price.

25
00:01:04,211 --> 00:01:04,958
When the price falls there,

26
00:01:04,958 --> 00:01:07,198
the effect reaches the shops of Zaveri Bazaar.

27
00:01:07,198 --> 00:01:08,450
Now think of a family.

28
00:01:08,450 --> 00:01:11,581
A few weeks ago they bought jewellery for their daughter's wedding.

29
00:01:11,581 --> 00:01:14,086
At a high price. If they sell that same jewellery by the tola today,

30
00:01:14,086 --> 00:01:16,277
its value will come out lower than before.

31
00:01:16,277 --> 00:01:17,928
But they did nothing unusual.

32
00:01:17,928 --> 00:01:20,404
For months gold had been rising steadily. A long,

33
00:01:20,404 --> 00:01:23,155
strong rally was going on. Everywhere people were saying,

34
00:01:23,155 --> 00:01:24,256
gold will go even higher.

35
00:01:24,256 --> 00:01:26,034
This is where the biggest misunderstanding is hiding.

36
00:01:26,034 --> 00:01:28,702
People understand 'safe' to mean 'will never fall'.

37
00:01:28,702 --> 00:01:29,887
But the market showed that

38
00:01:29,887 --> 00:01:32,258
even a safe thing can fall sharply.

39
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:34,098
So where did so much selling come from?

40
00:01:34,098 --> 00:01:37,470
Not from the small buyer on your street. From the big markets of the world,

41
00:01:37,470 --> 00:01:40,230
where a huge amount of goods is sold in a single day.

42
00:01:40,230 --> 00:01:41,752
And the real question is this.

43
00:01:41,752 --> 00:01:45,099
Who suddenly hit the brakes on such a long rally? The answer lies across the ocean,

44
00:01:45,099 --> 00:01:47,229
hidden in some figures from America.

45
00:01:47,229 --> 00:01:49,341
Second question: why did gold suddenly fall?

46
00:01:49,341 --> 00:01:53,212
This time, 3 blows hit together. Inflation, interest rates and the dollar.

47
00:01:53,212 --> 00:01:56,732
Let's understand them one by one, because they are linked to each other.

48
00:01:56,732 --> 00:01:57,719
The first blow, inflation.

49
00:01:57,719 --> 00:02:01,009
The new inflation figures in America came in hotter than expected.

50
00:02:01,009 --> 00:02:05,616
Meaning everyday things there were getting more expensive faster than predicted.

51
00:02:05,616 --> 00:02:09,045
Now America's central bank, which sets interest rates there,

52
00:02:09,045 --> 00:02:11,850
fights inflation. How? By keeping interest rates high.

53
00:02:11,850 --> 00:02:14,655
The market felt that interest rates won't come down soon.

54
00:02:14,655 --> 00:02:17,496
The second blow, interest rates. Understand one simple thing here.

55
00:02:17,496 --> 00:02:19,271
Gold pays no interest.

56
00:02:19,271 --> 00:02:23,177
It just lies quietly in the vault. No rent, no profit,

57
00:02:23,177 --> 00:02:24,597
just the play of price.

58
00:02:24,597 --> 00:02:27,838
Take an example. One shop pays rent every month.

59
00:02:27,838 --> 00:02:30,754
The other sits empty, no rent. If interest rises,

60
00:02:30,754 --> 00:02:33,347
people prefer the shop that pays rent.

61
00:02:33,347 --> 00:02:34,967
Gold is that empty shop.

62
00:02:34,967 --> 00:02:38,017
When bank FDs and government bonds start giving good interest,

63
00:02:38,017 --> 00:02:39,542
then holding gold feels costly.

64
00:02:39,542 --> 00:02:42,592
Big funds sell gold and put their money into things that pay interest.

65
00:02:42,592 --> 00:02:43,537
The third blow, the dollar.

66
00:02:43,537 --> 00:02:47,318
Expectations of inflation and higher interest rates made the dollar strong again.

67
00:02:47,318 --> 00:02:50,783
And remember, gold is priced in dollars.

68
00:02:50,783 --> 00:02:51,745
When the dollar got expensive,

69
00:02:51,745 --> 00:02:55,274
gold became more expensive for other countries. Europe, Japan,

70
00:02:55,274 --> 00:02:58,161
Indian buyers also held back a little. Demand weakened,

71
00:02:58,161 --> 00:02:59,444
and the price came down.

72
00:02:59,444 --> 00:03:02,093
Think of it like a seesaw. On one side sits the dollar,

73
00:03:02,093 --> 00:03:03,947
on the other side gold. When the dollar goes up,

74
00:03:03,947 --> 00:03:06,860
gold often comes down. This time too, the same happened.

75
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:09,056
And one last reason, the most human one.

76
00:03:09,056 --> 00:03:11,983
Those who had bought earlier during months of rally

77
00:03:11,983 --> 00:03:14,910
had a big profit piled up. On paper.

78
00:03:14,910 --> 00:03:16,374
Not yet in their pocket.

79
00:03:16,374 --> 00:03:17,601
As soon as the wind changed,

80
00:03:17,601 --> 00:03:20,056
they sold to put the profit in their pocket.

81
00:03:20,056 --> 00:03:22,817
This is called profit-booking. In other words, to save your earnings,

82
00:03:22,817 --> 00:03:24,351
selling after a rally.

83
00:03:24,351 --> 00:03:27,631
Then the dominoes started falling. One person sold, the price dropped. The price dropped,

84
00:03:27,631 --> 00:03:29,599
so others got scared. They sold too.

85
00:03:29,599 --> 00:03:33,207
Selling led to more selling, and the fall got sharper.

86
00:03:33,207 --> 00:03:36,198
But one thing seems strange. The book says,

87
00:03:36,198 --> 00:03:39,854
when inflation rises, gold goes up. This time inflation rose,

88
00:03:39,854 --> 00:03:42,180
and gold fell. Why did that happen?

89
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:45,935
Because this time the market feared interest rates more than inflation.

90
00:03:45,935 --> 00:03:47,643
Hot inflation means high interest rates.

91
00:03:47,643 --> 00:03:51,398
And high interest rates are heavy for gold. That was the real game.

92
00:03:51,398 --> 00:03:53,213
Now silver. According to Kitco News,

93
00:03:53,213 --> 00:03:55,934
silver fell more than 15 percent in a week.

94
00:03:55,934 --> 00:03:58,656
This was its worst week of this year.

95
00:03:58,656 --> 00:03:59,866
Much sharper than gold.

96
00:03:59,866 --> 00:04:03,449
Why? The first reason: the silver market is much smaller than the gold market.

97
00:04:03,449 --> 00:04:06,706
In a small pond, even one stone makes a big wave.

98
00:04:06,706 --> 00:04:08,334
A little selling, and a big jolt.

99
00:04:08,334 --> 00:04:10,914
The second reason: silver is not just jewellery. It is used in solar panels,

100
00:04:10,914 --> 00:04:13,817
electronics and factory work too.

101
00:04:13,817 --> 00:04:16,397
That's why its price swings from many directions.

102
00:04:16,397 --> 00:04:19,746
So silver is like gold's younger sister. It moves along with gold,

103
00:04:19,746 --> 00:04:22,790
but is more restless. In a rally, it runs faster than gold.

104
00:04:22,790 --> 00:04:25,226
And in a fall, it drops faster than gold too.

105
00:04:25,226 --> 00:04:27,009
In many homes there is a custom of saving silver coins,

106
00:04:27,009 --> 00:04:29,387
anklets and utensils.

107
00:04:29,387 --> 00:04:32,656
Those who bought silver at the top of the rally thinking it was 'cheap gold',

108
00:04:32,656 --> 00:04:34,142
felt the sharpest jolt.

109
00:04:34,142 --> 00:04:37,202
Now the big question: has such a fall happened before?

110
00:04:37,202 --> 00:04:40,568
Or is this the first time? History's answer is simple. Yes,

111
00:04:40,568 --> 00:04:42,404
it has happened. And it lasted long too.

112
00:04:42,404 --> 00:04:44,862
Remember 2013. According to BullionVault,

113
00:04:44,862 --> 00:04:48,374
in that whole year gold fell 30 percent in dollar terms.

114
00:04:48,374 --> 00:04:51,534
That is, almost a third of its price, gone in a single year.

115
00:04:51,534 --> 00:04:53,083
Back then too, the story was similar.

116
00:04:53,083 --> 00:04:56,800
America's central bank hinted at changing its money policy.

117
00:04:56,800 --> 00:05:00,207
Talk of ending cheap money came up, and gold started getting sold.

118
00:05:00,207 --> 00:05:03,548
The lesson of 2013 was clear. What the world calls 'safe',

119
00:05:03,548 --> 00:05:07,223
can also see a long fall. Not for weeks, but for months.

120
00:05:07,223 --> 00:05:09,228
When money policy turns.

121
00:05:09,228 --> 00:05:11,425
Those who panicked and sold at that time,

122
00:05:11,425 --> 00:05:14,249
turned a paper loss into a real one. Those who held on,

123
00:05:14,249 --> 00:05:17,387
had to wait. And that wait was not a short one.

124
00:05:17,387 --> 00:05:18,535
So gold doesn't break,

125
00:05:18,535 --> 00:05:20,830
but sometimes it goes into a long sleep.

126
00:05:20,830 --> 00:05:23,413
Nobody at the jewellery shop tells you this.

127
00:05:23,413 --> 00:05:25,708
There, only stories of rising prices are told.

128
00:05:25,708 --> 00:05:27,659
But one puzzle still remains.

129
00:05:27,659 --> 00:05:29,332
In times of fear, gold should go up.

130
00:05:29,332 --> 00:05:31,005
Then on the first day of the big shock,

131
00:05:31,005 --> 00:05:34,071
why is gold the first thing to be sold? The answer is surprising.

132
00:05:34,071 --> 00:05:35,543
Gold is called 'safe'.

133
00:05:35,543 --> 00:05:38,488
Then why did gold fall 24.6 percent in just 60 days?

134
00:05:38,488 --> 00:05:42,021
This question is in the mind of every family that holds gold today.

135
00:05:42,021 --> 00:05:43,860
According to commodity analyst Lukas Kuemmerle,

136
00:05:43,860 --> 00:05:47,539
such a big fall in 60 days has not come since 1982.

137
00:05:47,539 --> 00:05:49,685
That means not since your father's youth,

138
00:05:49,685 --> 00:05:51,218
has such a period been seen.

139
00:05:51,218 --> 00:05:53,694
So what is the real reason? A bitter truth.

140
00:05:53,694 --> 00:05:57,100
The world's big funds often borrow money and place very big bets on shares and

141
00:05:57,100 --> 00:05:59,576
other things.

142
00:05:59,576 --> 00:06:01,812
When the market suddenly takes a hit,

143
00:06:01,812 --> 00:06:04,366
the lender immediately demands money.

144
00:06:04,366 --> 00:06:07,560
This is called a margin call. It means 'deposit money right now,

145
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:08,518
or the deals are shut down'.

146
00:06:08,518 --> 00:06:11,710
Now what should the fund sell? If it sells fallen shares, there's a big loss.

147
00:06:11,710 --> 00:06:13,451
Some things don't sell right away at all.

148
00:06:13,451 --> 00:06:15,772
So it sells the thing that can be sold immediately,

149
00:06:15,772 --> 00:06:17,223
at a good price.

150
00:06:17,223 --> 00:06:18,581
That thing is gold.

151
00:06:18,581 --> 00:06:21,296
The easiest-selling commodity in the world.

152
00:06:21,296 --> 00:06:23,672
That's why in the first shock of a big fear,

153
00:06:23,672 --> 00:06:26,388
gold is often sold first. Out of compulsion.

154
00:06:26,388 --> 00:06:29,282
It means gold didn't fall because it became worthless.

155
00:06:29,282 --> 00:06:31,912
It was sold because it was the most useful.

156
00:06:31,912 --> 00:06:34,017
The most trustworthy, and the quickest to give money.

157
00:06:34,017 --> 00:06:36,721
So next time gold suddenly falls, remember this.

158
00:06:36,721 --> 00:06:38,343
Not every fall is proof of weakness.

159
00:06:38,343 --> 00:06:41,858
Sometimes it's just a sale to cover someone else's loss.

160
00:06:41,858 --> 00:06:45,347
The third question, and the most important. What now for your money?

161
00:06:45,347 --> 00:06:48,837
Gold affects each holder differently. Jewellery,

162
00:06:48,837 --> 00:06:51,628
gold loan, gold fund and government gold bond.

163
00:06:51,628 --> 00:06:54,325
First, those who hold jewellery. If you bought jewellery during a boom,

164
00:06:54,325 --> 00:06:56,123
its value will look lower today.

165
00:06:56,123 --> 00:06:58,220
But jewellery is often not meant for selling,

166
00:06:58,220 --> 00:07:00,318
it is for wearing and keeping safe.

167
00:07:00,318 --> 00:07:03,635
Remember one thing. Jewellery carries a making charge,

168
00:07:03,635 --> 00:07:07,284
that is, the cost of making it. When you sell, this is often not returned.

169
00:07:07,284 --> 00:07:09,606
So jewellery is less of an investment, more of a love for adornment.

170
00:07:09,606 --> 00:07:10,707
Second, those with a gold loan.

171
00:07:10,707 --> 00:07:13,183
You pledged your gold and took a loan from the bank.

172
00:07:13,183 --> 00:07:16,209
Pledging means keeping your gold with the bank in exchange for a loan.

173
00:07:16,209 --> 00:07:19,236
The bank gives a loan based on the gold price.

174
00:07:19,236 --> 00:07:20,040
Now the price has fallen,

175
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:23,525
so in the bank's eyes your pledged gold is worth less.

176
00:07:23,525 --> 00:07:27,278
In such a case, the bank may ask you to repay some money or keep more gold.

177
00:07:27,278 --> 00:07:31,397
So those with a gold loan should read their bank's messages and terms carefully.

178
00:07:31,397 --> 00:07:34,248
Don't panic, take steps only after understanding everything.

179
00:07:34,248 --> 00:07:35,832
This is the cheapest protection.

180
00:07:35,832 --> 00:07:37,048
Third, those with gold ETF.

181
00:07:37,048 --> 00:07:39,783
ETF means gold bought through the share market,

182
00:07:39,783 --> 00:07:42,214
without a safe and without fear of theft.

183
00:07:42,214 --> 00:07:44,645
Its price moves with gold every day.

184
00:07:44,645 --> 00:07:46,753
So if gold falls, your ETF falls too.

185
00:07:46,753 --> 00:07:48,335
This is not the fund's fault.

186
00:07:48,335 --> 00:07:50,707
The fund is doing exactly what it was meant to do.

187
00:07:50,707 --> 00:07:52,288
It moves like the shadow of gold.

188
00:07:52,288 --> 00:07:54,930
Fourth, those with SGB. SGB means Sovereign Gold Bond,

189
00:07:54,930 --> 00:07:56,252
the government's gold bond.

190
00:07:56,252 --> 00:07:59,555
Its price also goes up and down with gold.

191
00:07:59,555 --> 00:08:01,206
But there is one difference.

192
00:08:01,206 --> 00:08:05,046
On top of the gold price, SGB also pays 2.5 percent interest every year.

193
00:08:05,046 --> 00:08:07,789
Even when the price falls, this small interest keeps coming.

194
00:08:07,789 --> 00:08:09,435
In a fall, this is a bit of support.

195
00:08:09,435 --> 00:08:11,643
Now the biggest mistake, at the top.

196
00:08:11,643 --> 00:08:14,954
When everywhere people talk about 'gold at a record,'

197
00:08:14,954 --> 00:08:17,898
that's when most people rush in. Along with the crowd,

198
00:08:17,898 --> 00:08:19,370
at the highest price.

199
00:08:19,370 --> 00:08:22,502
And the mistake at the bottom. When the price falls and the news scares people,

200
00:08:22,502 --> 00:08:25,635
those same people panic and sell. They bought high,

201
00:08:25,635 --> 00:08:28,141
I sold at the bottom. The paper loss became a real loss.

202
00:08:28,141 --> 00:08:30,019
Third mistake: getting the meaning of 'safe' wrong.

203
00:08:30,019 --> 00:08:32,524
Safe means support over the long run.

204
00:08:32,524 --> 00:08:35,341
It doesn't mean the price will never fall.

205
00:08:35,341 --> 00:08:36,906
2013 taught exactly that.

206
00:08:36,906 --> 00:08:39,169
So what is the smart thing to do? First ask yourself,

207
00:08:39,169 --> 00:08:42,282
why are you holding gold? For a wedding, for hard times,

208
00:08:42,282 --> 00:08:45,394
or for quick profit? Your answer itself changes how you think.

209
00:08:45,394 --> 00:08:48,544
People who buy gold little by little, at different times,

210
00:08:48,544 --> 00:08:50,549
worry less about buying at the top.

211
00:08:50,549 --> 00:08:53,127
And in the heat of the news, rushing costs you heavily.

212
00:08:53,127 --> 00:08:54,559
This is not investment advice.

213
00:08:54,559 --> 00:08:58,288
Now, the question from the start. Why did the safest thing get sold first?

214
00:08:58,288 --> 00:09:01,678
Because in times of fear, the world needed cash immediately.

215
00:09:01,678 --> 00:09:03,712
And gold is the quickest thing to sell.

216
00:09:03,712 --> 00:09:06,361
In the next video, the terms of a gold loan, in simple language.

217
00:09:06,361 --> 00:09:08,215
And send this video to that friend

218
00:09:08,215 --> 00:09:10,069
who says gold never falls.

219
00:09:10,069 --> 00:09:12,322
Now, one simple question for you.

220
00:09:12,322 --> 00:09:16,828
Why do you have gold at home: wedding, hard times,

221
00:09:16,828 --> 00:09:20,433
or profit? Just write one word in the comments.
